  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "The final rules are a mixed outcome: S1 and S4 are within acceptable ranges, S5 is acceptable despite the recall trigger being exactly 8/100k (which would hit Halcyon's Ember 8), while S2 and S3 are weakened. S2 has a 5% review threshold but no automatic sales stop, and S3 sets a 24-month deadline for new units (beyond the 12-month acceptable limit) and a 6-year retrofit deadline. Northwind achieved its key goals: no public per-model disclosure, a 6-year retrofit, and no automatic sales ban for its Hearth 10; Halcyon secured customer test-result disclosure and a 36-month suppression deadline, but faces a mandatory recall for its Ember 8."
 },
